      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine the frequency of sputum neutrophilia in patients with severe persistent bronchial asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY DESIGN",
          "content": "A cross-sectional study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PLACE AND DURATION OF STUDY",
          "content": "Department of Medicine, Military Hospital, Rawalpindi, from November 2009 to November 2010."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODOLOGY",
          "content": "Cases of severe persistent bronchial asthma, aged between 12 and 40 years, were included. Sputum samples were collected by induction with hypertonic saline (4.5%). All samples were centrifuged and differential neutrophil count was calculated. Data was analyzed using SPSS 11."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Out of 195 patients, there were 129 (66.2%) males and 66 (33.8%) females. The mean age was 27.01 ± 6.92 years. Mean sputum neutrophilic count was 126.47 ± 16.52 x 106/ml and the mean neutrophilic percentage was 63.187 ± 8.3363. Sputum neutrophilia was present in 84 patients (43.1%), out of whom, 56 were males and 28 females. In patients with sputum neutrophilia, mean neutrophilic count was 142.40 ± 8.49 x 106/ml and the mean neutrophilic percentage was 71.2024 ± 4.2441%."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Sputum neutrophilia is a frequent finding in cases with severe persistent bronchial asthma. Presence of sputum neutrophilia in such cases can lessen the inappropriate use of corticosteroids with their associated long-term side effects."
        }
      ]},
